# Retro Arcade Design System - Cursor Rules

You are an expert in building retro arcade-style applications using Next.js 15, TypeScript, **Tailwind CSS v4**, and Framer Motion. You specialize in creating compact, mobile-first interfaces with authentic 80s/90s arcade aesthetics.

## Core Technology Stack

### Tailwind CSS v4 Setup
- **Always use Tailwind CSS v4** with the modern `@theme` and `@utility` syntax
- **Never use traditional tailwind.config.js** - all configuration is in `src/styles/globals.css`
- **CSS Variables**: All design tokens defined as CSS custom properties in the `@theme` block
- **Custom Utilities**: Retro-specific utilities defined with `@utility` syntax
- **Component Classes**: Defined in `@layer components` for complex reusable styles

### Globals.css Pattern (CRITICAL)
```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@plugin "tailwindcss-animate";

/* All theme configuration in @theme block */
@theme {
  /* CSS Variables for design tokens */
  --font-family-pixel: var(--font-pixeloid);
  --font-size-pixel-xs: 8px;
  --font-size-pixel-sm: 9px;
  --font-size-pixel-base: 10px;
  --color-primary: 0 212 255;
  --shadow-retro: 0 0 6px rgb(var(--color-primary));
  /* ... more variables */
}

/* Custom utilities with @utility */
@utility font-pixel {
  font-family: var(--font-family-pixel);
  image-rendering: pixelated;
}

@utility retro-glow {
  box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgb(var(--color-primary));
  text-shadow: 0 0 6px currentColor;
}

/* Component classes with @layer */
@layer components {
  .btn-retro {
    @apply bg-primary text-primary-foreground px-3 py-1.5;
    @apply border border-primary retro-glow pixel-perfect;
  }
}
```

### Design Token System
- **Font sizes**: Use CSS variables (`--font-size-pixel-xs: 8px`) accessed via utilities (`text-pixel-xs`)
- **Colors**: RGB space-separated values (`--color-primary: 0 212 255`) for opacity support
- **Shadows**: Predefined retro effects (`--shadow-retro`, `--shadow-pixel`) scaled proportionally
- **Spacing**: Compact mobile-first scale built into the theme

## Core Design Philosophy

### Retro Aesthetic Principles
- **Pixel-perfect rendering**: Use `pixel-perfect` utility class and crisp image rendering
- **Authentic color palette**: Bright cyan (#00d4ff) primary, warm amber secondary, dark backgrounds
- **Compact mobile-first**: Everything optimized for mobile screens with ~40% smaller sizing than typical designs
- **Proportional scaling**: All effects (glows, shadows, borders) scale together consistently
- **Arcade authenticity**: CRT effects, scanlines, retro typography, and neon glows

### Mobile-First Compaction Strategy
- **Font sizes**: Use pixel font system (text-pixel-xs: 8px, text-pixel-base: 10px, text-pixel-lg: 12px)
- **Spacing**: Prefer tight spacing (gap-1, gap-1.5, p-2, p-2.5) over large spacing
- **Icons**: Standard size 2.5x2.5 to 3x3, larger icons 4x4 for headers only
- **Touch targets**: Minimum h-6 for buttons while maintaining visual compactness
- **Borders**: Use 1px borders as default, 2px only for special emphasis

## Component Patterns

### Naming Convention
- Prefix all custom components with "Retro" (e.g., RetroButton, RetroCard)
- Use descriptive variant names: "arcade", "pixel", "medieval", "crt", "neon"
- Size variants: "xs", "sm", "default", "lg" (no "xl" unless absolutely necessary)

### Required Props Pattern
```typescript
interface RetroComponentProps
  extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>,
    VariantProps<typeof componentVariants> {
  withScanlines?: boolean;
  withCrtEffect?: boolean;
  glow?: "none" | "subtle" | "medium" | "intense";
}
```

### Variant Structure Template
```typescript
const retroComponentVariants = cva(
  "pixel-perfect font-pixel transition-all duration-200", // Base classes
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        arcade: "bg-arcade-screen border border-primary shadow-arcade",
        pixel: "bg-card border border-primary shadow-pixel", 
        medieval: "bg-medieval-stone border border-medieval-gold",
        crt: "bg-arcade-screen border border-primary shadow-crt",
      },
      size: {
        sm: "p-2 gap-1 text-pixel-xs",
        default: "p-2.5 gap-1.5 text-pixel-sm", 
        lg: "p-3 gap-2 text-pixel-base",
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: "arcade",
      size: "default",
    },
  }
);
```

## Styling Guidelines

### Typography System (Always use these classes)
```css
/* Always use pixel font system - defined in globals.css @theme */
font-pixel text-pixel-xs   /* 8px - smallest text */
font-pixel text-pixel-sm   /* 9px - secondary text */
font-pixel text-pixel-base /* 10px - body text */
font-pixel text-pixel-lg   /* 12px - headings */

/* Special fonts for variety */
font-bokor    /* Medieval/fantasy style */
font-medieval /* Cormorant Unicase for elegance */
```

### Color Usage (CSS Variables from @theme)
```css
/* Primary arcade colors - using CSS variables */
text-primary        /* rgb(var(--color-primary)) - Bright cyan */
text-primary/80     /* Dimmed for secondary text */
text-primary/60     /* Further dimmed for labels */

/* Status colors */
text-success        /* rgb(var(--color-success)) - Bright green */
text-warning        /* rgb(var(--color-warning)) - Bright yellow */
text-destructive    /* rgb(var(--color-destructive)) - Bright red */

/* Backgrounds */
bg-arcade-screen    /* Main arcade background */
bg-card            /* Card backgrounds */
bg-arcade-bezel    /* Darker accent background */
```

### Custom Utility Classes (Defined in globals.css)
```css
/* Use these custom utilities - all defined with @utility */
pixel-perfect       /* Image rendering optimization */
retro-glow         /* Text and box glow effect */
retro-glow-lg      /* Larger glow effect */
pixel-shadow       /* Pixelated drop shadow */
pixel-shadow-lg    /* Larger pixelated shadow */
arcade-shadow      /* Inset + outer glow combination */
crt-shadow         /* CRT screen inset shadow */
retro-border       /* Glowing border effect */
```

### Spacing Scale (Mobile-Compact - from @theme)
```css
/* Gaps and padding - use sparingly */
gap-0.5, gap-1, gap-1.5, gap-2     /* Prefer smaller gaps */
p-1, p-1.5, p-2, p-2.5, p-3       /* Compact padding scale */
m-1, m-2, m-3, m-4                 /* Minimal margins */

/* Avoid large spacing unless absolutely necessary */
/* gap-4+, p-4+, m-6+ should be rare */
```

## Extending the Design System

### Adding New Utilities (globals.css)
```css
/* Add new retro utilities with @utility syntax */
@utility my-new-effect {
  /* CSS properties using CSS variables */
  box-shadow: 0 0 var(--shadow-size) rgb(var(--color-primary));
  border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-primary));
}
```

### Adding New Design Tokens (@theme block)
```css
@theme {
  /* Add new CSS variables in the @theme block */
  --shadow-my-effect: 0 0 8px rgb(var(--color-primary));
  --color-my-variant: 255 100 150;
  --font-size-my-size: 11px;
}
```

### Adding Component Classes (@layer components)
```css
@layer components {
  .my-retro-component {
    @apply bg-primary text-primary-foreground;
    @apply border border-primary pixel-perfect;
    @apply font-pixel text-pixel-sm;
    /* Can mix @apply with CSS variables */
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-retro);
  }
}
```

## Component Creation Checklist

### For Every New Retro Component:
1. **Use Tailwind v4 syntax** - No config file, everything in globals.css
2. **Leverage CSS variables** from the @theme block
3. **Use custom utilities** defined with @utility
4. **Start with cva variants** for consistent API
5. **Include mobile-first sizing** (default should be compact)
6. **Add pixel-perfect class** to base styles
7. **Support glow prop** for interactive feedback
8. **Include withScanlines option** for arcade authenticity
9. **Use forwardRef pattern** for proper DOM access
10. **Add proper TypeScript interfaces** extending HTML attributes
11. **Test with smaller icons** (2.5x2.5, 3x3) before using larger ones

### Adding New Theme Values
```css
/* Always extend the @theme block in globals.css */
@theme {
  /* New color */
  --color-my-new-color: 150 255 100;
  
  /* New shadow effect */
  --shadow-my-effect: 0 0 8px rgb(var(--color-my-new-color));
  
  /* New font size */
  --font-size-pixel-custom: 11px;
  --line-height-pixel-custom: 14px;
}

/* Then create utility if needed */
@utility text-pixel-custom {
  font-size: var(--font-size-pixel-custom);
  line-height: var(--line-height-pixel-custom);
}
```

## Animation Guidelines
```typescript
/* Prefer subtle, retro-appropriate animations using CSS variables */
transition-all duration-200        /* Fast transitions */
hover:scale-105                   /* Subtle hover growth */
active:scale-95                   /* Press feedback */
animate-pulse                     /* For status indicators */

/* Framer Motion for complex animations */
initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 20 }}
animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
transition={{ duration: 0.3 }}
```

## File Structure Requirements

### globals.css Structure (MANDATORY)
```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@plugin "tailwindcss-animate";

/* 1. Theme configuration with CSS variables */
@theme {
  /* All design tokens here */
}

/* 2. Custom utility classes */
@utility utility-name {
  /* Custom CSS */
}

/* 3. Component classes */
@layer components {
  .component-class {
    @apply /* tailwind classes */;
  }
}

/* 4. Keyframe animations */
@keyframes animation-name {
  /* Animation steps */
}

/* 5. Base styles */
body {
  /* Global styles using CSS variables */
}
```

## Common Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ Don't Do This:
```jsx
// Using non-pixel fonts
<span className="font-sans text-base">

// Large spacing (old patterns)
<div className="p-6 gap-4">

// Hardcoded colors instead of CSS variables
<div style={{ color: '#00d4ff' }}>

// Creating tailwind.config.js (v4 uses globals.css)

// Ignoring the custom utility classes
<div className="shadow-lg"> {/* Use shadow-retro instead */}
```

### ✅ Do This Instead:
```jsx
// Use pixel font system
<span className="font-pixel text-pixel-base">

// Compact spacing
<div className="p-2.5 gap-1.5">

// Use CSS variable colors through utilities
<div className="text-primary">

// Add new utilities to globals.css @utility blocks

// Use custom retro utilities
<div className="shadow-retro">
```

